@* "Need an Entra application?" — a compact help card; the structured administrator instructions open on demand. Identifiers appear only here. *@
<aside class="gsx-callout" aria-labelledby="gss-admin-title" data-testid="gss-registration">
    <div class="gsx-callout-head">
        <div>
            <strong id="gss-admin-title">Need an Entra application?</strong>
            <p class="gsx-help-text">Your administrator must register a public-client application and grant the required delegated Azure DevOps permission.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="gsx-actions">
            <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" aria-expanded="@(Setup.InstructionsOpen ? "true" : "false")" aria-controls="gss-admin-steps"
                    @onclick="() => Setup.InstructionsOpen = !Setup.InstructionsOpen" data-testid="gss-instructions-toggle">@(Setup.InstructionsOpen ? "Hide setup instructions" : "View setup instructions")</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" @onclick="@(() => Setup.CopyAsync(GitSourcesPresentation.RegistrationRequest, "instructions"))" data-testid="gss-registration-copy">
                @(Setup.Copied == "instructions" ? "Copied" : "Copy instructions")</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    @if (Setup.InstructionsOpen)
    {
        <ol id="gss-admin-steps" class="gsx-instructions" data-testid="gss-registration-text">
            <li><strong>App registration</strong><span>Register an application (or choose BirkNext's). Supported account types: this organizational directory only.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Authentication platform</strong><span>Add the platform "Mobile and desktop applications". Allow public client flows (device code). No client secret or certificate.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Redirect URI</strong><span><code>@GitSourcesPresentation.RedirectUri</code></span></li>
            <li><strong>API permissions</strong><span>Azure DevOps (<code class="gsx-wrap">@GitSourcesPresentation.AzureDevOpsResourceId</code>) → delegated <code>user_impersonation</code>. Optional for Azure Environment Analysis: Azure Service Management → <code>user_impersonation</code>.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Consent</strong><span>Grant admin consent if users in the tenant may not consent themselves.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Information to send back</strong><span>The Application (client) ID and the Directory (tenant) ID. The person using BirkNext also needs Azure DevOps access (Basic or Stakeholder) and read permission on the repositories.</span></li>
        </ol>
    }
</aside>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public GitSourcesSetupState Setup { get; set; } = default!;
}
